Troglodyte Pidgin is the primitive language of the cave-dwelling troglodytes.
It consists of hissing sounds, clicks, and guttural croaks that echo well
in the subterranean passages these creatures call home.

The language is relatively simple compared to surface tongues, focusing on
immediate needs such as hunting, territory, and warnings of danger. However,
its unusual phonetics make it challenging for surface dwellers to learn.

Knowledge of Troglodyte Pidgin can be valuable when exploring deep caves
and underground complexes where these reptilian humanoids dwell, allowing
for potential communication or at least understanding of their intentions.

